# FilmMend Me — Project Rules

Flutter cross-platform app for mood-based movie recommendations, watchlists, and profiles.
**Mental model:** UI shell over **TMDB** (read-only movie data) + **Firebase** (auth, profiles, watchlists, remote config).

Reference: `docs/ai-context.md` for full architecture summary.

---

## Architecture (do not fight it)

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
|-------|----------|----------------|
| Presentation | `lib/features/*/presentation/` | Screens only — no `domain/` or `data/` subfolders |
| Services | `lib/services/` | Firebase + TMDB I/O, business logic for APIs |
| Models | `lib/models/` | `MovieModel`, `UserModel`, JSON/Firestore parsing |
| Core | `lib/core/` | Router, theme, shared widgets, Firebase guards |

**Intentionally absent** (do not introduce unless explicitly requested):
- Provider, Riverpod, Bloc, GetIt, or other DI/state libraries
- Repository/use-case layers
- Router-level auth redirects

Screens call services directly: `TmdbService()`, `AuthService()`, `WatchlistService()`.

---

## Folder Structure

```
lib/
├── main.dart              # Entry: .env load, error widget, runApp
├── app.dart               # Firebase bootstrap, MaterialApp.router
├── firebase_options.dart  # Generated/injected Firebase config
├── core/
│   ├── firebase/firebase_safe.dart
│   ├── router/            # router.dart, app_shell.dart, route_names.dart
│   ├── theme/             # app_colors, app_theme, app_constants, app_text_styles
│   └── widgets/           # Shared UI; export via widgets.dart barrel
├── features/
│   └── <feature>/presentation/<feature>_screen.dart
├── models/
└── services/
```

### Where to put new code

| Change | Location |
|--------|----------|
| New screen | `lib/features/<name>/presentation/<name>_screen.dart` |
| New route | `lib/core/router/router.dart` + `route_names.dart` |
| Reusable widget (2+ features) | `lib/core/widgets/` + export in `widgets.dart` |
| API / Firebase logic | `lib/services/<name>_service.dart` |
| Data type | `lib/models/<name>_model.dart` |
| Colors / theme tokens | `lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart` or `app_theme.dart` |

