## Firebase & Auth

### Safe access (required)

Never call `FirebaseAuth.instance` directly in UI without guards. Use:

```dart
import '../../../core/firebase/firebase_safe.dart';

safeCurrentUser()           // User? — null if Firebase not ready
safeAuthStateChanges()      // Stream<User?>
```

### Auth flows

| State | UI component |
|-------|--------------|
| Not logged in | `LoginRequiredView` (watchlist, profile) |
| Logged in, email unverified | `VerificationRequiredView` (watchlist add actions) |
| Firebase errors | `AuthService.friendlyError(e)` for `FirebaseAuthException` |

### Firestore schema (respect in services + rules)

```
users/{uid}                    # displayName, email, createdAt, photoUrl
users/{uid}/watchlist/{movieId}  # movieId, title, posterPath, rating, genres, runtime, addedAt
app_config/recommendation_rules  # moodGenres map — read-only for clients
```

Update `firestore.rules` when changing document shapes. Rules enforce field sets and owner-only access.

